# Data — never commit real/sensitive data (species locations, personal data).
# The folder and its README are tracked; everything else inside is ignored.
data/*
!data/README.md

# --- Client data formats, wherever they land -------------------------------
# `data/*` above covers the intended location. These patterns catch the same
# formats anywhere in the tree — a workbook saved next to a notebook, an extract
# dropped into api/, an archive copied in from Downloads.
#
# The unconditional CI data-guard jobs fail if one of these is TRACKED. These
# rules stop it being staged in the first place; the guard catches a
# `git add -f` or a rename that dodges a pattern. Both, because either alone has
# a hole.
#
# If you genuinely need to commit one (a synthetic fixture), force-add it AND add
# its path to ALLOWED in scripts/guard_no_data_files.py with the reason.
*.xls
*.xlsx
*.xlsm
*.xlsb
*.ods
*.csv
*.tsv
*.psv
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.gz
*.bz2
*.xz
*.parquet
*.feather
*.dta
*.sav
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
